CRANE (Chemistry and Radiation in Atmospheres with Nonlinear Evolution)

-photochem works with conda environment
-pyharp is independent of environment, just need to  pip install pyharp

verions:

pyharp: 1.6.8
https://github.com/chengcli/pyharp/

photochem: 0.6.2
https://github.com/Nicholaswogan/photochem



setting up RT requires you to adhere to some specific conventions.

in the RT yaml file:
1. the species list must be ordered in the same way as your harp_keys/pchem keys in your crane-config file
2. the jit aerosol opacity files must be called {species}-{band}.pt (species in lowercase)
3. the jit cia aerosol opacity files must be called {species1}_{species2}-{band} (species in lowercase)

in the crane-config file:
1. see #1 above
2. the aerosol input file list must be ordered in the same way that the aerosols are ordered in the harp_keys list


by default, when you simulate RT out of range of your known input aerosol/CIA data, the attn coeff is set to 0 for extrapolation. 
